E AX3084 1065-struct-marker.ax:7:9-18 struct-marker "word struct `TwoFields` declares 2 fields, and a word holds exactly one" #"refused here" !"a word struct is one machine word, not a block (docs/memory-model.md MM-VAL-10a)" ?"give it one field, `(slot : Int)`: a word struct IS its one field, so a second one has nowhere to live"
E AX3084 1065-struct-marker.ax:12:8-9 struct-marker "field `x` of word struct `Mutable` is `mut`" #"refused here" !"a word struct has no block a field store could reach" ?"drop `mut`: a word struct is a value, and a store would change only the copy it was made on"
E AX3084 1065-struct-marker.ax:15:4-5 struct-marker "field `x` of word struct `NotAWord` is not an `Int`" #"refused here" !"a `String`, a `Vec` or a record is a reference, and a word that held one would take no share of it" ?"type the field `Int`: a word struct holds one machine word, and `Int` is the type that is one"
E AX3084 1065-struct-marker.ax:17:9-15 struct-marker "word struct `Params` takes type parameters" #"refused here" !"a word takes no share and so has no evidence a type argument could describe" ?"drop the parameters: a word carries no type argument"
E AX3084 1065-struct-marker.ax:20:9-19 struct-marker "struct `SharedHeap` is `shared` but not a `word`" #"refused here" !"a heap struct is a counted block, and `axiom_retain` is a plain load-add-store: two bindings touching one count lose an increment and free a block still named (MM-PAR-6)" ?"add `word`, or drop `shared`: only a word may be shared between concurrent bindings"
E AX3084 1065-struct-marker.ax:23:20-24 struct-marker "`word` is written twice" #"refused here" !"a marker says one thing about the struct, and saying it twice says nothing more" ?"write each marker once"
E AX3084 1065-struct-marker.ax:26:17-23 struct-marker "`packed` is not a struct marker" #"refused here" !"the markers come between the name and the first field: `(struct Chan word shared (slot : Int))`" ?"a struct takes `word`, which makes it one machine word rather than a heap block, and `shared`, which lets a `parallel` binding capture a `word`; anything else after the struct's name is refused"
